{"name":"Duckling","hex":"#fcb057","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"duckling","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A young duck.","A young female duck."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/duckling"}],"entries":[{"title":"Duckling (Louie)","blocks":[{"text":"\"Duckling\" is the eleventh episode of the second season of the American comedy-drama television series Louie. It is the 24th overall episode of the series and was written and directed by Louis C.K., who also serves as the lead actor. It was released on FX on August 25, 2011."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Duckling_(Louie)","wikidata":"Q114551071"},{"title":"Duckling (software)","blocks":[{"text":"Duckling, the collaboration environment software suite for e-Science, is an open-source software suite developed by the Collaboration Environment Research Center of Computer Network Information Center of the Chinese Academy of Sciences to meet the rapid progress of the Chinese Academy of Sciences’ e-Science activities. The goals of Duckling include integrating various resources such as digital hardware, software and data, and building a high efficient and easy-to-use environment over Internet for scientists distributed in different positions to enable a new type scientific action mode."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Duckling_(software)","wikidata":"Q5311532"},{"title":"Duck","blocks":[{"text":"Duck is the common name for numerous species of waterfowl in the family Anatidae. Ducks are generally smaller and shorter-necked than swans and geese, which are members of the same family. Divided among several subfamilies, they are a form taxon; they do not represent a monophyletic group, since swans and geese are not considered ducks. Ducks are mostly aquatic birds, and may be found in both fresh water and sea water."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bf/Bucephala-albeola-010.jpg/330px-Bucephala-albeola-010.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Duck","wikidata":"Q3736439"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/82/Pacific_Black_Ducks_on_pond_ducking.jpg/500px-Pacific_Black_Ducks_on_pond_ducking.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/82/Pacific_Black_Ducks_on_pond_ducking.jpg/1280px-Pacific_Black_Ducks_on_pond_ducking.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/82/Pacific_Black_Ducks_on_pond_ducking.jpg/500px-Pacific_Black_Ducks_on_pond_ducking.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Pacific black duck displaying the characteristic upending \"duck\"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3APacific_Black_Ducks_on_pond_ducking.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/78/Mallard-drake-chicago-march-2024.jpg/500px-Mallard-drake-chicago-march-2024.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/78/Mallard-drake-chicago-march-2024.jpg/1280px-Mallard-drake-chicago-march-2024.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/78/Mallard-drake-chicago-march-2024.jpg/500px-Mallard-drake-chicago-march-2024.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Male mallard.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMallard-drake-chicago-march-2024.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7d/Wood-ducks-male-female-chicago-march-2024.jpg/500px-Wood-ducks-male-female-chicago-march-2024.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thum